  "body": "## Finding description\n\nIn both `_processLimitBidOrder` and `_processLimitAskOrder`, the code tries to detect zero-cost trades with a bitwise test instead of a logical zero check:\n\n```solidity\n// Bid path\nif (baseTokenAmountReceived != quoteTokenAmountSent && baseTokenAmountReceived & quoteTokenAmountSent == 0) {\n    revert ZeroCostTrade();\n}\n\n// Ask path\nif (baseTokenAmountSent != quoteTokenAmountReceived && baseTokenAmountSent & quoteTokenAmountReceived == 0) {\n    revert ZeroCostTrade();\n}\n```\n\nThe intended condition is to revert if either side of the trade is 0.\nBut the implementation is wrong, as `a & b == 0` is not equivalent to `(a == 0 || b == 0)`. Many non-zero integer pairs satisfy a & b == 0 (See PoC for the values used). As a result, the code will trigger false positives and valid limit orders that partially fill will revert with `ZeroCostTrade()`.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny partial-fill of limit orders where the computed base and quote transfer amounts are both non-zero but where `a & b == 0` will revert.\n\nThis even introduces a griefing vector where an attacker could create an order to match a victim's one to trigger the `(a & b) == 0 ` condition on purpose and make their limit post fail.\n\nNote that this affects both ask and bid limit paths.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nUse a zero check instead of the bitwise operations.\n\n```solidity\n// In _processLimitBidOrder\nif (baseTokenAmountReceived == 0 || quoteTokenAmountSent == 0) {\n    revert ZeroCostTrade();\n}\n\n// In _processLimitAskOrder\nif (baseTokenAmountSent == 0 || quoteTokenAmountReceived == 0) {\n    revert ZeroCostTrade();\n}\n```\nThis is what is already done in `_processFillBidOrder` and `_processFillAskOrder`",
  "proof_of_concept": "## PoC\n\nPaste this file in `PoC.t.sol` (imports are important)\n\nTwo crossing limit orders that should match actually revert with `ZeroCostTrade()` even though both legs are non-zero — proving the bitwise check is wrong and causes false positives.\n\n```solidity\n\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"test/harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {Book, BookLib, Limit, MarketConfig, MarketSettings} from \"contracts/clob/types/Book.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager, SettingsParams} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {Side, Order} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n\n     function test_submissionValidityBitWiseZeroTrade() public {\n        ICLOB abCLOBContract = ICLOB(abCLOB);\n        address quote = address(tokenA); // A = quote\n        address base  = address(tokenB); // B = base\n\n        // @audit - Seed ASK liquidity at the crafted price so incoming BID crosses\n        address askMaker = makeAddr(\"askMaker\");\n        ERC20Harness(base).mint(askMaker, 100 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(askMaker);\n        ERC20Harness(base).approve(address(accountManager), 100 ether);\n        accountManager.deposit(askMaker, base, 100 ether);\n        abCLOBContract.postLimitOrder(\n            askMaker,\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase: 100 ether,\n                price: 3.8395 ether,                  // crafted price (multiple of tickSize)\n                cancelTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 1 days),\n                side: Side.SELL,\n                clientOrderId: 0,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n\n        //@audit because (base & quote) == 0 -> the call reverts \n        address bidder = makeAddr(\"bidder\");\n        vm.prank(bidder);\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes4(0xd8a00083)); // ZeroCostTrade()\n        abCLOBContract.postLimitOrder(\n            bidder,\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase: 0.005 ether,\n                price: 3.8395 ether,                 // crosses best ask\n                cancelTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 1 days),\n                side: Side.BUY,\n                clientOrderId: 0,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n            })\n        );\n    }\n\n}\n```",
